# openHC — Control4 CA-1 controller (i.MX6 SoloLite, board codename "emmet").
#
# Unlike ea1/ea3 (ea-common), this board has NO family base defconfig (same as
# ioxv1): build/build.sh's default case feeds this file to Buildroot on its
# own. Split out a ca-common when a second CA-series board lands — every
# value here is either SoC-generic or CA-1-specific, and inventing a family for
# one board would just add a level of indirection with nothing in it.
#
# What this board is (confirmed on a live rev-4 unit — docs/ca1-recon.md):
#
#   * i.MX6SL: ONE Cortex-A9 (ARMv7-A, VFPv3-D32 + NEON), 1 GB RAM.
#   * 16 MB SPI-NOR (S25FL128S on ecspi2) holds U-Boot 2014.04 + a recovery
#     kernel; 3.7 GB eMMC (usdhc2) holds vfat kernel / ext4 rootfs / ext4 recfs.
#   * Stock U-Boot, unlocked console, writable environment, and NO secure boot
#     (HAB fuse open, U-Boot's CSF slot zero-filled, kernel loaded with a plain
#     bootz). We can boot our own kernel without touching flash.
#   * Radios: ZM5304 Z-Wave on UART4, an EM35x Zigbee NCP on UART5, and a
#     Realtek RTL8723BS Wi-Fi/BT combo on SDIO (usdhc1).
#   * NO companion IO-MCU. The rear RS-232/RS-485 port is a host UART (UART3)
#     in front of a GPIO-configured transceiver.
#
# STATUS: pre-boot. This builds a toolchain, kernel and rootfs; nobody has
# booted it on hardware yet. Unlike the DM355 the SoC needs no resurrection
# patches — mainline supports i.MX6SL — so the risk here is the board DTS
# (board/ca1/linux/c4-imx6sl-ca1.dts), not the kernel.

# --- arch: i.MX6SL = single Cortex-A9, ARMv7-A, VFPv3-D32 + NEON, EABIhf ---
# cpuinfo reports "vfpv3 ... vfpd32", i.e. the full 32 double registers, so
# plain VFPV3 rather than the D16 variant. Hard float: there is an FPU, use it.
BR2_arm=y
BR2_cortex_a9=y
BR2_ARM_ENABLE_NEON=y
BR2_ARM_ENABLE_VFP=y
BR2_ARM_FPU_VFPV3=y
BR2_ARM_EABIHF=y

BR2_OPTIMIZE_S=y
# musl, matching every other board in this tree.
BR2_TOOLCHAIN_BUILDROOT_MUSL=y

# --- init / login ---
# Console is ttymxc0 @115200 (U-Boot passes console=ttymxc0,115200).
BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_HOSTNAME="openhc-ca1"
BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_ISSUE="openHC Control4 CA-1 (kernel-up)"
BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_ROOT_PASSWD="openhc"
BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_GETTY_PORT="ttymxc0"
BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_GETTY_BAUDRATE_115200=y
BR2_ROOTFS_DEVICE_CREATION_DYNAMIC_MDEV=y

# --- kernel: mainline stable, same version as the rest of the tree ---
# i.MX6SL is fully supported upstream, so this is a stock defconfig plus a
# board DTS — no SoC patches, no BR2_GLOBAL_PATCH_DIR. That is the whole reason
# this board is a soft target compared to the DM355.
BR2_LINUX_KERNEL=y
BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_CUSTOM_VERSION=y
BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_CUSTOM_VERSION_VALUE="7.1.8"
BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_USE_DEFCONFIG=y
BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_DEFCONFIG="imx_v6_v7"
BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_CONFIG_FRAGMENT_FILES="$(BR2_EXTERNAL_OPENHC_PATH)/ca1/linux/ca1.fragment"

# U-Boot boots this with `bootz`, so a raw zImage — no uImage wrap (ioxv1) and
# no CEFDK container (EA family).
BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_ZIMAGE=y

# Our own board DTS, reconstructed from the vendor DTB for a mainline kernel.
BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_DTS_SUPPORT=y
BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_CUSTOM_DTS_PATH="$(BR2_EXTERNAL_OPENHC_PATH)/ca1/linux/c4-imx6sl-ca1.dts"

# --- rootfs: ext4 on eMMC p2 (persistent) — NOT an embedded initramfs ---
# We booted openHC from a RAM initramfs for bring-up, but that path is exhausted:
# the whole rootfs is embedded in the zImage and decompressed below the DTB at
# 0x83000000, so it must stay under ~40 MB decompressed. The lean image (18.5 MB
# cpio) fit; adding even ttyd (23 MB cpio) tipped it over and hung "Starting
# kernel" again. Python/Node for the web UI + zigbee/zwave servers never had a
# chance. So the real system lives on the eMMC ext4 rootfs (mmcblk1p2), the
# kernel mounts it directly (root=/dev/mmcblk1p2, see post-image.sh), and the
# zImage carries NO initramfs — which also makes it small and permanently ends
# the DTB-overwrite class of bug. Writing p2 replaces the stock Control4 rootfs;
# factory restore rebuilds it from p3, so it stays recoverable.
# BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_INITRAMFS is intentionally OFF.
BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_EXT2=y
BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_EXT2_4=y
# Sized for the full stack (python3 web API now, node zigbee2mqtt/zwave-js next);
# resized to fill p2 (1.9 GB) with resize2fs at install time.
BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_EXT2_SIZE="768M"

# --- reachability + on-target tools ---
BR2_PACKAGE_DROPBEAR=y
BR2_PACKAGE_BUSYBOX_SHOW_OTHERS=y
# SPI-NOR inspection. Note the bring-up path never writes this chip — U-Boot
# and both environment copies live there.
BR2_PACKAGE_MTD=y
# The radio resets and the seven RS-485 transceiver lines, by name, from
# userspace on the chardev ABI. See rootfs-overlay/etc/init.d/S30gpio.
BR2_PACKAGE_LIBGPIOD=y
BR2_PACKAGE_LIBGPIOD_TOOLS=y
# fw_printenv/fw_setenv talk to the U-Boot environment in SPI-NOR, which is how
# the boot path is steered on this board; mkimage builds the boot.scr that
# stock bootcmd sources off the eMMC FAT partition.
BR2_PACKAGE_UBOOT_TOOLS=y
BR2_PACKAGE_UBOOT_TOOLS_MKIMAGE=y
BR2_PACKAGE_UBOOT_TOOLS_FWPRINTENV=y
# Host mkimage: post-image.sh uses it to build the boot.scr that stock bootcmd
# sources off the eMMC vfat partition. Without this the image still builds, but
# post-image.sh warns and skips the boot script.
BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_UBOOT_TOOLS=y
# Writing the kernel/DTB/boot.scr onto the vfat "kernel" partition.
BR2_PACKAGE_DOSFSTOOLS=y
BR2_PACKAGE_DOSFSTOOLS_FSCK_FAT=y

# --- Wi-Fi: in-tree rtl8723bs (staging) replaces the vendor 8723bs.ko ---
# The stock image carries a 1.25 MB out-of-tree module; mainline has had
# drivers/staging/rtl8723bs since v4.12.
#
# Firmware is fiddlier than it looks, checked against Buildroot 2024.02.9 and
# Linux 7.1.8 rather than assumed:
#
#   * Bluetooth is covered — RTL_87XX_BT ships rtl_bt/rtl8723bs_fw.bin and
#     rtl_bt/rtl8723bs_config-OBDA8723.bin, which is what btrtl asks for.
#   * Wi-Fi is NOT. rtl8723b_hal_init.c does request_firmware() on
#     "rtlwifi/rtl8723bs_nic.bin" (there is no embedded firmware array any
#     more), and that exact file is missing from RTL_87XX's file list — it
#     ships rtl8723bs_bt.bin and rtl8723bu_nic.bin, but not rtl8723bs_nic.bin.
#
# The file IS present in the linux-firmware tarball Buildroot already
# downloads, so post-build.sh lifts it out of the extracted source rather than
# vendoring a blob here or adding a second download. Wi-Fi is not the
# bring-up reachability path either way — S40net brings up eth0 only.
BR2_PACKAGE_LINUX_FIRMWARE=y
BR2_PACKAGE_LINUX_FIRMWARE_RTL_87XX=y
BR2_PACKAGE_LINUX_FIRMWARE_RTL_87XX_BT=y
BR2_ROOTFS_POST_BUILD_SCRIPT="$(BR2_EXTERNAL_OPENHC_PATH)/ca1/post-build.sh"
BR2_PACKAGE_WPA_SUPPLICANT=y
BR2_PACKAGE_WPA_SUPPLICANT_NL80211=y
BR2_PACKAGE_WPA_SUPPLICANT_CLI=y
# 2.4 GHz-only radio, but cfg80211 refuses to pick a channel plan at all
# without a regulatory.db, warning "failed to load regulatory.db" at boot.
BR2_PACKAGE_WIRELESS_REGDB=y
# Setup AP (openhc-ca1-<mac>) when eth0 has no carrier — S41wifi-ap in the
# rootfs overlay. eth0 stays the only client-mode reachability path; nothing
# here joins an existing network.
BR2_PACKAGE_HOSTAPD=y
BR2_PACKAGE_DNSMASQ=y

# --- mDNS identity: avahi (no D-Bus, light), matching the other boards ---
BR2_PACKAGE_AVAHI=y
BR2_PACKAGE_AVAHI_DAEMON=y

# --- rear RS-232/485 port exposed over the network (RFC2217/telnet-com-port) ---
# ser2net's own S50ser2net init script ships with the package; it just needs a
# config, which lives in rootfs-overlay/etc/ser2net/ser2net.yaml. Direction
# stays whatever the DTS gpio-hogs set at boot (RS-232 today) — runtime mode
# switching needs those hogs converted to a real consumer first (see the DTS).
BR2_PACKAGE_SER2NET=y

# --- MQTT broker for zigbee2mqtt; also useful standalone for the Z-Wave side ---
# Buildroot 2024.02.9's mosquitto-2.0.19 package fails to apply its own bundled
# 0001-Revert-Fix-NetBSD-build.patch against the tarball currently served at
# mosquitto.org ("Reversed (or previously applied) patch detected" on several
# hunks) — a stock package/upstream-tarball mismatch, not a local config issue.
# Revisit when the Zigbee/Z-Wave work actually needs a broker.
# BR2_PACKAGE_MOSQUITTO=y

# C++ toolchain — needed by Node.js and ser2net's gensio C++ bindings.
BR2_TOOLCHAIN_BUILDROOT_CXX=y

# The web dashboard + API is the Rust ohc-webd binary (packages/), cross-built
# on the host with the React UI embedded and dropped into the overlay by
# packages/build.sh — so no python3/ttyd interpreter or per-port terminal daemon
# is needed on the target. board/common S90ohcweb just runs the one binary.

# --- Node.js: runtime for zigbee2mqtt / zwave-js-server on the ext4 rootfs ---
# npm included so the servers install on-target. V8 is a heavy compile — see the
# build.sh JLEVEL note / bump Docker's VM RAM if it OOMs.
BR2_PACKAGE_NODEJS=y
BR2_PACKAGE_NODEJS_NPM=y

# --- rootfs overlay + image publishing ---
# board/common first: the shared Rust webd starter (S90ohcweb). ca1's own
# overlay (Wi-Fi AP fallback, net, ser2net sample) comes after so it can override.
BR2_ROOTFS_OVERLAY="$(BR2_EXTERNAL_OPENHC_PATH)/common/rootfs-overlay $(BR2_EXTERNAL_OPENHC_PATH)/ca1/rootfs-overlay"
BR2_ROOTFS_POST_IMAGE_SCRIPT="$(BR2_EXTERNAL_OPENHC_PATH)/ca1/post-image.sh"
BR2_ROOTFS_POST_SCRIPT_ARGS="ca1"
